    "body": "Hi everybody,\r\n\r\nI am working on a plugin that will provide the possibility to schedule messages about a new issue on Facebook. In order to get a Facebook application I have to add the relevant parts about cookies and Facebook to the privacy policy. I think that's no problem for me to do it by hand, but it would be challenging for journals when they would want to use the plugin themselves. Also I think there other plugins that would face the same issue.\r\n\r\nI thought about the situation that it would be great when plugins could provide the necessary information for the privacy policy. The best knowledge about the collection and use of personal information have the authors of the plugins. When the plugin would provide this knowledge journal managers would be able to use plugins that need you to extend your privacy policy without worrying that they might miss an important part for their privacy policy.\r\n\r\nI also have thought about other ways to achieve this. Like putting the information into the plugin documentation so that you can copy it into your privacy policy yourself. But I think in the case of plugin updates it might be forgotten to update the privacy policy after updating the plugin.\r\n\r\nTo solve this I would propose a change to `AboutSiteHandler.inc.php`. By adding a hook call right before the `$templateMgr->assign` plugins could add additional information to the privacy policy.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
